\
# Final Submission Summary\
\
*   **Strongest Findings:** The necessity of a "Staple-first" classification for the East African market to ensure user adoption.\
*   **High-Confidence Areas:** Global beverage standards (Coffee/Alcohol) and International Allergen lists.\
*   **Weak Evidence:** Specific sub-categorization of Central African forest-sourced ingredients (e.g., specific varieties of Chikwangue).\
*   **Key Recommendation:** Implement a **Faceted Search** (Filter by: Occasion > Category > Diet) rather than a deep nested folder structure.\
*   **Further Investigation:** Integration of "Carbon Footprint" or "Nutritional Scores" as automated tags based on ingredient data.}